- A venerable millionaire, mad for her.

779
00:28:33,834 --> 00:28:35,156
The mask you sent me was the one that

780
00:28:35,156 --> 00:28:38,473
Christine wore at his
masked ball last year.

781
00:28:38,473 --> 00:28:40,009
- Good.

782
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:41,301
We'll start with him.

783
00:28:41,301 --> 00:28:43,251
- It's already done.

784
00:28:43,251 --> 00:28:45,641
Senor Lamas is receiving
attorney Bryan Cooper

785
00:28:45,641 --> 00:28:47,006
tomorrow at 10.

786
00:28:47,006 --> 00:28:48,286
- Fine.

787
00:28:48,286 --> 00:28:49,609
I think we'll get along all right.

788
00:28:49,609 --> 00:28:50,442
- Anything else?

789
00:28:50,442 --> 00:28:52,425
- Yes, one little thing.

790
00:28:52,425 --> 00:28:53,662
Are you a natural redhead?

791
00:28:53,662 --> 00:28:54,601
- [Crow] Are you a natural blackhead?

792
00:28:54,601 --> 00:28:57,684
- You'll have to take my word for it.

793
00:28:58,867 --> 00:28:59,700
For now.

794
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:00,533
- [Joel] Wait are you saying,

795
00:29:00,533 --> 00:29:01,555
does that mean I'm,

796
00:29:01,555 --> 00:29:03,134
uh, bye.

797
00:29:03,134 --> 00:29:04,798
- [Crow] Oh flat, I get it.

798
00:29:04,798 --> 00:29:05,907
- You know what I always said,

799
00:29:05,907 --> 00:29:07,059
dames are like safes,

800
00:29:07,059 --> 00:29:08,467
some guys know their secrets

801
00:29:08,467 --> 00:29:10,387
and some guys don't.

802
00:29:10,387 --> 00:29:11,795
- Is that what you've always said?

803
00:29:11,795 --> 00:29:12,990
- Yeah.

804
00:29:12,990 --> 00:29:14,787
- I think you've spent too
much time cracking safes.

805
00:29:14,787 --> 00:29:17,518
(Tom mimics drumbeat

806
00:29:17,518 --> 00:29:20,419
- [Joel] Why there's Amsterdam.

807
00:29:20,419 --> 00:29:21,657
- [Tom] Hey Maury!

808
00:29:21,657 --> 00:29:22,490
Oh, oh.

809
00:29:25,838 --> 00:29:28,483
- [Joel] Hey his eyes have a zoom feature.

810
00:29:28,483 --> 00:29:30,745
- I think it's time we made
a couple of social calls.

811
00:29:30,745 --> 00:29:32,281
Let's start with Christine Brueder.

812
00:29:32,281 --> 00:29:33,524
- All right.

813
00:29:33,524 --> 00:29:35,822
- [Tom] Now why did he bring this guy?

814
00:29:35,822 --> 00:29:38,553
- I made you an outfit
special for the occasion.

815
00:29:38,553 --> 00:29:40,217
- [Crow] It's a bulletproof teddy.

816
00:29:40,217 --> 00:29:42,917
- It's the coolest thing going
and absolutely bulletproof.

817
00:29:42,917 --> 00:29:45,118
(chuckles)

818
00:29:45,118 --> 00:29:47,566
- [Joel] This won't go
with my black skirt.

819
00:29:47,566 --> 00:29:48,462
- Well what did you want, huh?

820
00:29:48,462 --> 00:29:49,742
Buttons and bows?

821
00:29:49,742 --> 00:29:51,619
- [Tom] Oh there's a satin
tap pant that goes with it.

822
00:29:51,619 --> 00:29:54,354
- Ah and while we're on
the subject of buttons--

823
00:29:54,354 --> 00:29:55,420
- [Tom] They shoulda brought Jack Weston.

824
00:29:55,420 --> 00:29:56,883
- Looks just like the others.

825
00:29:56,883 --> 00:29:59,187
- [Joel] He's kind of a
white trash Q, isn't he?

826
00:29:59,187 --> 00:30:01,107
- [Crow] Yeah.

827
00:30:01,107 --> 00:30:04,051
It's ingenious, it closes your jacket.

828
00:30:04,051 --> 00:30:05,051
- All right.

829
00:30:06,014 --> 00:30:06,847
- [Tom] Okay now,

830
00:30:06,847 --> 00:30:07,806
I'm the escaped convict

831
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,223
and you're the warden's wife.

832
00:30:11,390 --> 00:30:12,243
- Perfect fit, huh?

833
00:30:12,243 --> 00:30:13,076
- [Joel] It's a little tight in the busom.

834
00:30:13,076 --> 00:30:14,425
- And what's this for?

835
00:30:14,425 --> 00:30:15,258
- This

836
00:30:19,587 --> 00:30:20,753
is the safety.

837
00:30:20,753 --> 00:30:23,097
- [Crow] Are they going steady now?

838
00:30:23,097 --> 00:30:24,097
- That's it.

839
00:30:27,491 --> 00:30:29,174
- It seems to work all right.

840
00:30:29,174 --> 00:30:31,262
- Hey, now tell me I'm not a genius.

841
00:30:31,262 --> 00:30:32,190
- [Bryan] All right.

842
00:30:32,190 --> 00:30:33,054
You're not a genius.

843
00:30:33,054 --> 00:30:34,937
- [Joel] Hey I walked right into that one.

844
00:30:34,937 --> 00:30:36,270
- [Tom] Ba boom.

845
00:30:39,374 --> 00:30:42,238
- [Crow] Well now he's
secret agent Superloiterer.

846
00:30:42,238 --> 00:30:44,158
- [Man] There you are.

847
00:30:44,158 --> 00:30:46,575
- [Tom] Laramie, is that you?

848
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:48,916
- [Joel] Andy Capp's gained weight.

849
00:30:48,916 --> 00:30:49,795
- Is it busted?

850
00:30:49,795 --> 00:30:50,962
- No it isn't.

851
00:30:54,446 --> 00:30:56,946
(Tom humming)

852
00:30:58,414 --> 00:31:01,414
- [Crow] I know what you're wearing.

853
00:31:02,295 --> 00:31:03,961
- [Tom] Boy, they've
seen a lot of apartments

854
00:31:03,961 --> 00:31:06,267
on this trip, haven't they?

855
00:31:06,267 --> 00:31:09,434
- [Joel] Hey it's Rula Lenska's place.

856
00:31:11,257 --> 00:31:12,835
- [Crow] I hope this isn't
like a John Waters film

857
00:31:12,835 --> 00:31:15,523
and they lick all the furniture.

858
00:31:15,523 --> 00:31:17,856
- [Tom] Tub Taylor on vibes.

859
00:31:20,558 --> 00:31:22,990
- [Crow] Hm, Broytans.

860
00:31:22,990 --> 00:31:25,907
- [Joel] Here, try opening the top.

861
00:31:26,745 --> 00:31:27,662
Gimme that.

862
00:31:30,286 --> 00:31:31,119
- [Tom] Well I,

863
00:31:31,119 --> 00:31:32,952
I loosened it for ya'.

864
00:31:33,827 --> 00:31:36,697
- [Joel] Oh I didn't get you anything.

865
00:31:36,697 --> 00:31:40,323
- [Crow] He's wearing the
Phil Harris collection.

866
00:31:40,323 --> 00:31:43,740
- [Joel] Oh no, it's grandma's brag book.

867
00:31:46,467 --> 00:31:49,184
- Here, you keep the
picture of Vic Tayback.

868
00:31:49,184 --> 00:31:52,707
(mysterious music)

869
00:31:52,707 --> 00:31:54,874
(humming)

870
00:32:01,710 --> 00:32:04,483
- [Joel] I'm just gonna
freshen up in here, okay?

871
00:32:04,483 --> 00:32:06,429
- [Crow] I enjoy being a girl.

872
00:32:06,429 --> 00:32:07,262
Huh, oh.

873
00:32:13,161 --> 00:32:14,546
- [Tom] Ladies and
gentlemen, Mother Teresa.

874
00:32:14,546 --> 00:32:17,718
- [Crow] (gasps) Hey.
- [Tom] Maybe not.

875
00:32:17,718 --> 00:32:19,571
- Are you looking for somewhere to sleep,

876
00:32:19,571 --> 00:32:20,638
or something else?

877
00:32:20,638 --> 00:32:24,313
- [Bryan] No, I was feeling a
little bit lonely, that's all.

878
00:32:24,313 --> 00:32:26,617
- Did you think I would keep you company?

879
00:32:26,617 --> 00:32:27,769
- Something like that, yes.

880
00:32:27,769 --> 00:32:28,921
- [Crow] Do you have a towel I can borrow?

881
00:32:28,921 --> 00:32:31,395
- That might have been your idea

882
00:32:31,395 --> 00:32:33,401
but you've come to the wrong address.

883
00:32:33,401 --> 00:32:34,339
Give me my robe.

884
00:32:34,339 --> 00:32:35,875
- Oh, sure.

885
00:32:35,875 --> 00:32:37,027
- [Woman] Stay where you are.

886
00:32:37,027 --> 00:32:38,527
- [Joel] Lay down.

887
00:32:44,409 --> 00:32:46,371
- Would you turn your
face to the wall please?

888
00:32:46,371 --> 00:32:47,481
- Oh no, I don't mind turning.

889
00:32:47,481 --> 00:32:49,648
I like all kinds of games.

890
00:32:50,723 --> 00:32:53,977
(Babyface whistles)
- [Crow] Oooh pretty lady.

891
00:32:53,977 --> 00:32:55,673
- [Woman] And who is this?

892
00:32:55,673 --> 00:32:57,123
- Who him?

893
00:32:57,123 --> 00:33:00,384
Why I never saw that
man before in my life.

894
00:33:00,384 --> 00:33:01,646
You should be ashamed of yourself.

895
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:02,755
What do you think you're doing in this

896
00:33:02,755 --> 00:33:03,694
nice lady's bedroom?

897
00:33:03,694 --> 00:33:05,742
Why don't you get out
of here, you stupid oaf?

898
00:33:05,742 --> 00:33:06,990
Get out of here.

899
00:33:06,990 --> 00:33:08,910
- Okay, okay, I'm going.

900
00:33:08,910 --> 00:33:10,414
I got the wrong door.

901
00:33:10,414 --> 00:33:11,769
- [Tom] Allen and Rossi,
ladies and gentlemen,

902
00:33:11,769 --> 00:33:13,910
Allen and Rossi.
- [Crow] With Julie Budd.

903
00:33:13,910 --> 00:33:15,449
- [Woman] And you, what
are you waiting for?

904
00:33:15,449 --> 00:33:17,113
- Well, a little information
if you don't mind.

905
00:33:17,113 --> 00:33:17,946
Do you uh,

906
00:33:17,946 --> 00:33:19,630
happen to know this girl, hm?

907
00:33:19,630 --> 00:33:20,915
- Why yes, it's Christine Brueder,

908
00:33:20,915 --> 00:33:22,750
she's living here with me.

909
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:23,731
What do you want to know for?

910
00:33:23,731 --> 00:33:24,670
- I happen to be a lawyer.

911
00:33:24,670 --> 00:33:26,942
I'm here on a very important
inheritance problem.

912
00:33:26,942 --> 00:33:27,856
My name is Bryan Cooper.

913
00:33:27,856 --> 00:33:29,001
- [Joel] Cooper like the hockey equipment.

914
00:33:29,001 --> 00:33:31,177
- I'm sorry but Christine's
not in Amsterdam.

915
00:33:31,177 --> 00:33:32,670
She's away with some friends.

916
00:33:32,670 --> 00:33:34,163
- Do you happen to know
when she'll be getting back?

917
00:33:34,163 --> 00:33:35,657
- I imagine if she's having fun,

918
00:33:35,657 --> 00:33:36,809
it will be a while.

919
00:33:36,809 --> 00:33:37,961
- Well I'd like to see
her some day when she's

920
00:33:37,961 --> 00:33:40,265
not so busy amusing herself.

921
00:33:40,265 --> 00:33:43,593
- But please, next time ring the bell.

922
00:33:43,593 --> 00:33:45,822
Leave me your address in
case my friend returns.

923
00:33:45,822 --> 00:33:47,266
- [Tom] They talk like
a Speed Racer cartoon.

924
00:33:47,266 --> 00:33:48,809
- Sure, sure, here you are.

925
00:33:48,809 --> 00:33:50,892
Hope I see you again, hm?

926
00:33:54,867 --> 00:33:56,745
- [Crow] Hey, secret agent's crossed out

927
00:33:56,745 --> 00:33:59,091
and lawyer's written in.

928
00:33:59,091 --> 00:33:59,924
Hm.

929
00:34:01,865 --> 00:34:04,032
(dialing)

930
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:09,166
- [Joel] You're on Larry King Live,

931
00:34:09,166 --> 00:34:11,470
Europe, you're on the air.

932
00:34:11,470 --> 00:34:12,451
- Please Alex,

933
00:34:12,451 --> 00:34:14,713
you've got to listen carefully.

934
00:34:14,713 --> 00:34:17,780
- [Joel] Yeah, I know,
I look like Spike Jonze.

935
00:34:17,780 --> 00:34:19,197
- You must do it.

936
00:34:20,435 --> 00:34:22,102
He's very dangerous.

937
00:34:23,038 --> 00:34:24,713
That's right, just do what I tell you.

938
00:34:24,713 --> 00:34:26,291
- [Crow] Go to the window.

939
00:34:26,291 --> 00:34:27,187
- Yes you must.

940
00:34:27,187 --> 00:34:28,595
- [Joel] Increase your bust.

941
00:34:28,595 --> 00:34:29,747
- [Tom] Oh enough spy crap,

942
00:34:29,747 --> 00:34:31,326
time to see Amsterdam.

943
00:34:31,326 --> 00:34:32,905
(laughs)

944
00:34:32,905 --> 00:34:35,405
(happy music)

945
00:34:40,243 --> 00:34:41,694
Brideshead revisited.

946
00:34:41,694 --> 00:34:42,889
To the manor Borne.

947
00:34:42,889 --> 00:34:44,425
Upstairs, downstairs,

948
00:34:44,425 --> 00:34:46,046
the magician with Bill Bixby.

949
00:34:46,046 --> 00:34:47,326
- [Crow] Huh?

950
00:34:47,326 --> 00:34:48,905
- [Man] That's the last picture of her

951
00:34:48,905 --> 00:34:50,185
over a year ago.

952
00:34:50,185 --> 00:34:52,602
- [Crow] She has a beard now.

953
00:34:53,906 --> 00:34:54,739
- [Joel] Mario Cuomo?

954
00:34:54,739 --> 00:34:56,947
- Christine and I were very good friends.

955
00:34:56,947 --> 00:34:57,886
- [Crow] Nobody in this movie knows

956
00:34:57,886 --> 00:34:59,763
when to stop decorating.

957
00:34:59,763 --> 00:35:01,171
- [Tom] Uh, you got any art here?

958
00:35:01,171 --> 00:35:02,366
- Then all of a sudden-

959
00:35:02,366 --> 00:35:03,199
- [Joel] Kablooey.

960
00:35:03,199 --> 00:35:05,907
- The girl I thought I
knew became a stranger.

961
00:35:05,907 --> 00:35:07,955
Moody, withdrawn.

962
00:35:07,955 --> 00:35:11,667
I found out she'd begun to drug herself.

963
00:35:11,667 --> 00:35:13,763
I tried to get her to stop it.

964
00:35:13,763 --> 00:35:15,001
She wouldn't.

965
00:35:15,001 --> 00:35:17,049
She booked passage for America.

966
00:35:17,049 --> 00:35:18,846
Now you say that she's returned.

967
00:35:18,846 --> 00:35:20,894
- [Crow] But good luck
with your pledge drive.

968
00:35:20,894 --> 00:35:23,881
- I'd have expected her to telephone.

969
00:35:23,881 --> 00:35:25,886
- [Tom] Wanna give this a try?

970
00:35:25,886 --> 00:35:28,451
- Are you having an auction
masquerade this year?

971
00:35:28,451 --> 00:35:30,585
- Yes, I wouldn't miss it for anything.

972
00:35:30,585 --> 00:35:31,566
- [Joel] Except cheese.

973
00:35:31,566 --> 00:35:33,145
- This year I'm offering a canvas

974
00:35:33,145 --> 00:35:35,278
that's rather extraordinary.

975
00:35:35,278 --> 00:35:36,942
You're a lover of the arts, aren't you?

976
00:35:36,942 --> 00:35:38,947
- Well I'm afraid all I
can afford is to look.

977
00:35:38,947 --> 00:35:39,801
(laughs)

978
00:35:39,801 --> 00:35:40,634
- [Tom] Get out!

979
00:35:40,634 --> 00:35:42,531
- May I show you my lute
player by Franz Haus?

980
00:35:42,531 --> 00:35:44,409
- [Tom] No, no, no, no, please.

981
00:35:44,409 --> 00:35:47,310
- It's the prize of the entire collection.

982
00:35:47,310 --> 00:35:48,889
- [Tom] Emo avec lute.

983
00:35:48,889 --> 00:35:51,577
- It's worth over a million Dutch florins.

984
00:35:51,577 --> 00:35:54,062
But I expect it to
raise considerably more.

985
00:35:54,062 --> 00:35:57,262
No, it'll all be for charity.

986
00:35:57,262 --> 00:35:59,139
I think you'll find this interesting.

987
00:35:59,139 --> 00:36:00,806
- [Crow] But stupid.

988
00:36:01,998 --> 00:36:02,831
- Over here.

989
00:36:02,831 --> 00:36:04,498
- [Tom] Get in this.

990
00:36:05,806 --> 00:36:08,025
- It's an international
hospital for babies

991
00:36:08,025 --> 00:36:09,219
with malnutrition.

992
00:36:09,219 --> 00:36:10,286
- [Joel] And pancakes.

993
00:36:10,286 --> 00:36:11,950
- Art is a marvelous thing.

994
00:36:11,950 --> 00:36:13,367
But saving lives,

995
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:15,875
children's lives especially--

996
00:36:15,875 --> 00:36:16,708
- [Crow] It's not that good.

997
00:36:16,708 --> 00:36:17,923
- Is more important.

998
00:36:17,923 --> 00:36:20,953
That's why I always try to
make my auctions spectacular.

999
00:36:20,953 --> 00:36:22,713
It appeals to everyone's vanity.

1000
00:36:22,713 --> 00:36:23,779
- [Joel] And Apollonia too.

1001
00:36:23,779 --> 00:36:26,041
- Generosity, as you know, is rare.

1002
00:36:26,041 --> 00:36:27,075
Vanity on the other hand,

1003
00:36:27,075 --> 00:36:28,446
is a rather common trait.

1004
00:36:28,446 --> 00:36:29,731
- Yes, but the vain like to be seen

1005
00:36:29,731 --> 00:36:31,923
and your parties are
masquerades, aren't they?

1006
00:36:31,923 --> 00:36:32,756
(Tom chuckles)

1007
00:36:32,756 --> 00:36:35,977
- That makes it a little more exciting.

1008
00:36:35,977 --> 00:36:37,982
The losers can remain anonymous.

1009
00:36:37,982 --> 00:36:39,347
- [Crow] And the winners
remain bottomless.

1010
00:36:39,347 --> 00:36:41,950
- And when the winner removes his mask,

1011
00:36:41,950 --> 00:36:44,126
there is usually applause

1012
00:36:44,126 --> 00:36:46,104
and his vanity is satisfied completely.

1013
00:36:46,104 --> 00:36:47,246
- Oh that's most ingenious,

1014
00:36:47,246 --> 00:36:48,665
but I'm afraid we've taken
up too much of your time.

1015
00:36:48,665 --> 00:36:49,498
- Not at all.

1016
00:36:49,498 --> 00:36:52,104
Very grateful to you for your visit.

1017
00:36:52,104 --> 00:36:53,310
- [Joel] Um, what else, oh.

1018
00:36:53,310 --> 00:36:55,118
- We're all anxious to locate Christine.

1019
00:36:55,118 --> 00:36:56,825
I've every hope we can.

1020
00:36:56,825 --> 00:36:57,934
We'll keep in touch.

1021
00:36:57,934 --> 00:36:58,915
- [Woman] You've been most kind.

1022
00:36:58,915 --> 00:36:59,748
- And thank you.

1023
00:36:59,748 --> 00:37:02,126
- [Tom] Oh and let us know
when the Pavarotti comes in.

1024
00:37:02,126 --> 00:37:04,526
- There's a famous hotel in Wallendam.

1025
00:37:04,526 --> 00:37:06,963
- [Joel] Called the Shady Rest.

1026
00:37:06,963 --> 00:37:09,481
- Christine used to go
there frequently, I recall.

1027
00:37:09,481 --> 00:37:10,718
You might try that.

1028
00:37:10,718 --> 00:37:11,699
- Thank you.

1029
00:37:11,699 --> 00:37:13,065
- [Crow] But don't eat
the almonds in the bar,

1030
00:37:13,065 --> 00:37:15,241
they charge you 10 bucks for them.

1031
00:37:15,241 --> 00:37:16,270
- You look a little discouraged.

1032
00:37:16,270 --> 00:37:18,361
- Looks like I brought
you on a wild goose chase.

1033
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:19,555
- Oh there's nothing to worry about.

1034
