01:15:44,198 --> 01:15:45,231
- [Tom] In another half an hour,

2032
01:15:45,231 --> 01:15:47,897
they'll be hungry for Chinese.

2033
01:15:47,897 --> 01:15:52,803
- [Crow] Oh wow, so this is
what the other half does, hm?

2034
01:15:52,803 --> 01:15:54,126
- Thank you, here we go.

2035
01:15:54,126 --> 01:15:56,209
- [Joel] It's booze call.

2036
01:15:59,971 --> 01:16:01,849
- Here's to those big brown eyes.

2037
01:16:01,849 --> 01:16:04,449
- [Tom] Yeah, here's
to your death big guy.

2038
01:16:04,449 --> 01:16:07,011
(high-pitched beeping)

2039
01:16:07,011 --> 01:16:10,096
- [Crow] Waitress, there's
a squeeze toy in my drink.

2040
01:16:10,096 --> 01:16:11,619
- Miss, miss!

2041
01:16:11,619 --> 01:16:13,795
I just remembered, I don't drink.

2042
01:16:13,795 --> 01:16:15,795
- [Tom] Whoa, close one.

2043
01:16:21,817 --> 01:16:24,633
- And now the most precious
treasure of the collection.

2044
01:16:24,633 --> 01:16:26,937
The magnificent lute player by Franz Haus.

2045
01:16:26,937 --> 01:16:28,985
I ask you ladies and
gentlemen to open the bidding

2046
01:16:28,985 --> 01:16:31,094
at one million five
hundred thousand florins.

2047
01:16:31,094 --> 01:16:31,927
- [Voiceover] Two million.

2048
01:16:31,927 --> 01:16:33,389
- [Tom] Lower.

2049
01:16:33,389 --> 01:16:34,313
- Ah two million.

2050
01:16:34,313 --> 01:16:36,663
I'm offered two million
once, two million twice and--

2051
01:16:36,663 --> 01:16:37,496
- [Voiceover] Three million.

2052
01:16:37,496 --> 01:16:38,755
- I'll offer you three and a half.

2053
01:16:38,755 --> 01:16:41,170
- [Auctioneer] Anyone
top three and a half?

2054
01:16:41,170 --> 01:16:42,126
- Six million.

2055
01:16:42,126 --> 01:16:43,662
- [Joel] A bajillion.

2056
01:16:43,662 --> 01:16:45,667
- [Crow] A kazillion, jillion,

2057
01:16:45,667 --> 01:16:47,006
upteen berdillion.

2058
01:16:47,006 --> 01:16:49,038
- That sir, I consider a personal insult.

2059
01:16:49,038 --> 01:16:50,105
- [Crow] Hi.

2060
01:16:50,105 --> 01:16:51,994
- [Tom] Oh yeah?

2061
01:16:51,994 --> 01:16:54,297
- Teach you a lesson.

2062
01:16:54,297 --> 01:16:56,558
- [Tom] Oh that sir, I
consider a personal punch.

2063
01:16:56,558 --> 01:16:57,923
- [Joel] Oh they've been
given a drink that turns

2064
01:16:57,923 --> 01:16:59,246
them into shriners.

2065
01:16:59,246 --> 01:17:00,840
- [Crow] Oh how horrible.

2066
01:17:00,840 --> 01:17:01,814
- Will you look at that?

2067
01:17:01,814 --> 01:17:03,064
- [Tom] Hoohoo!

2068
01:17:04,590 --> 01:17:06,211
(Tom laughs)

2069
01:17:06,211 --> 01:17:08,942
- [Crow] Hey everybody, let's boink.

2070
01:17:08,942 --> 01:17:11,586
- [Tom] It's a good night at Eau Bar.

2071
01:17:11,586 --> 01:17:13,635
(people laughing)

2072
01:17:13,635 --> 01:17:15,171
- [Crow] Ah, Louis the 14th, good one.

2073
01:17:15,171 --> 01:17:17,171
That's two or three mil.

2074
01:17:19,993 --> 01:17:23,193
- They're all just behaving like animals.

2075
01:17:23,193 --> 01:17:26,094
- [Joel] Hey bring back
the funny pictures.

2076
01:17:26,094 --> 01:17:27,886
- What you have seen is
only an example of the

2077
01:17:27,886 --> 01:17:30,019
efficiency of Synchron 2.

2078
01:17:30,019 --> 01:17:31,769
Whenever we choose to use it,

2079
01:17:31,769 --> 01:17:33,902
then victory will be ours.

2080
01:17:33,902 --> 01:17:34,883
- [Tom] Victory over what?

2081
01:17:34,883 --> 01:17:35,950
- Yes, gentlemen,

2082
01:17:35,950 --> 01:17:37,657
the victory will indeed be ours.

2083
01:17:37,657 --> 01:17:39,235
- [Crow] Ours the victory will be.

2084
01:17:39,235 --> 01:17:41,923
- We are going to change
the course of human life.

2085
01:17:41,923 --> 01:17:44,611
The antidote, Anti-Synchron

2086
01:17:44,611 --> 01:17:46,446
is known to us and to us alone.

2087
01:17:46,446 --> 01:17:47,342
- [Tom] Oh and I told my brother

2088
01:17:47,342 --> 01:17:48,281
but he said he wouldn't tell anyone.

2089
01:17:48,281 --> 01:17:50,371
- And with it we shall gain world mastery.

2090
01:17:50,371 --> 01:17:52,206
Foreign agents have tried to stop us,

2091
01:17:52,206 --> 01:17:54,297
notably the invincible Super Dragon.

2092
01:17:54,297 --> 01:17:55,619
They have been killed.

2093
01:17:55,619 --> 01:17:58,691
The false Ming vases are
now in our possession.

2094
01:17:58,691 --> 01:18:00,355
The vases have been sent here

2095
01:18:00,355 --> 01:18:01,763
from our factories in India.

2096
01:18:01,763 --> 01:18:03,214
- [Joel] We have factories in India?

2097
01:18:03,214 --> 01:18:06,112
- The drug is mixed with
a porcelain in such a way

2098
01:18:06,112 --> 01:18:08,163
that no one could ever detect it.

2099
01:18:08,163 --> 01:18:10,254
- [Crow] But still it's
delicious and low cal.

2100
01:18:10,254 --> 01:18:13,070
- In six of them, there is a
sufficient quantity of the drug

2101
01:18:13,070 --> 01:18:15,203
to bring to a conclusion

2102
01:18:15,203 --> 01:18:17,700
the first phase of the operation.

2103
01:18:17,700 --> 01:18:18,745
- [Joel] Phase 1,

2104
01:18:18,745 --> 01:18:20,579
swingin' sixties style party.

2105
01:18:20,579 --> 01:18:21,570
- [Crow] Whoo!

2106
01:18:21,570 --> 01:18:23,011
(crowd laughing)

2107
01:18:23,011 --> 01:18:24,163
- [Tom] You're on.

2108
01:18:24,163 --> 01:18:27,554
- [Crow] Oh nothing,
nothing. (nervously chuckles)

2109
01:18:27,554 --> 01:18:28,495
- [Tom] That's odd,

2110
01:18:28,495 --> 01:18:31,118
they're playing Twister where
there ain't no Twister board.

2111
01:18:31,118 --> 01:18:33,035
- [Joel] Doris Day, no!

2112
01:18:35,001 --> 01:18:36,668
- [Tom] It's Sarina.

2113
01:18:37,603 --> 01:18:40,353
- [Crow] I'll fix that, Samantha.

2114
01:18:41,821 --> 01:18:43,790
- [Tom] Hello, I am Louis Jordan.

2115
01:18:43,790 --> 01:18:44,771
I turn ague,

2116
01:18:44,771 --> 01:18:46,435
I walk, I have a gun

2117
01:18:46,435 --> 01:18:48,768
and still I am Louis Jordan.

2118
01:18:49,678 --> 01:18:51,394
Pardon me while I hit the snack table.

2119
01:18:51,394 --> 01:18:52,566
I'm Louis Jordan.

2120
01:18:52,566 --> 01:18:54,003
- Don't make a sound, get moving.

2121
01:18:54,003 --> 01:18:55,170
- [Joel] Beep.

2122
01:18:57,929 --> 01:18:59,635
- Brilliant.

2123
01:18:59,635 --> 01:19:01,328
Our compliments.

2124
01:19:01,328 --> 01:19:03,865
- [Crow] Mother always calls
during these meetings, sorry.

2125
01:19:03,865 --> 01:19:05,273
- I can at last announce to you that

2126
01:19:05,273 --> 01:19:07,851
Professor Kruger has been able
to find a-- (audio cuts off)

2127
01:19:07,851 --> 01:19:09,201
- [Tom] A what?
- In one hour we will have it.

2128
01:19:09,201 --> 01:19:11,763
Gentlemen, await instructions.

2129
01:19:11,763 --> 01:19:13,171
- [Joel] Uh, can I ask
why we're at this meeting?

2130
01:19:13,171 --> 01:19:14,707
- We will adjourn.

2131
01:19:14,707 --> 01:19:17,248
- [Crow] Let's get some of
that kooky champagne, huh?

2132
01:19:17,248 --> 01:19:20,171
(moaning)

2133
01:19:20,171 --> 01:19:21,150
- [Tom] Ah, crimeny,

2134
01:19:21,150 --> 01:19:23,326
Dave's doing his human
cake roll thing again.

2135
01:19:23,326 --> 01:19:25,971
You gotta jump on him
and squirt the jelly out.

2136
01:19:25,971 --> 01:19:28,275
- [Crow] I'm a naughty
little cheesy blintz.

2137
01:19:28,275 --> 01:19:30,358
- [Tom] Cut it out, Dave.

2138
01:19:31,683 --> 01:19:33,822
- Get to the embassy right
away, contact Coleman.

2139
01:19:33,822 --> 01:19:35,742
The Ming vases are leaving tonight

2140
01:19:35,742 --> 01:19:37,027
and must be stopped

2141
01:19:37,027 --> 01:19:38,947
and the names and
addresses of all the buyers

2142
01:19:38,947 --> 01:19:40,581
investigated, I'll take care of Comfort.

2143
01:19:40,581 --> 01:19:42,921
- [Tom] Oh, um, oh I, oh yeah.

2144
01:19:42,921 --> 01:19:45,421
(happy music)

2145
01:19:49,391 --> 01:19:50,624
- [Tom] Hi, where you
goin'? What are you doin'?

2146
01:19:50,624 --> 01:19:51,990
Just wanna walk with you is all.

2147
01:19:51,990 --> 01:19:53,161
Nice dress.

2148
01:19:53,161 --> 01:19:54,057
- Comfort?

2149
01:19:54,057 --> 01:19:55,724
- [Joel] Comfort me.

2150
01:19:58,793 --> 01:20:01,376
(woman laughs)

2151
01:20:04,512 --> 01:20:07,801
- [Crow] Those guys are
still hopped up on vase.

2152
01:20:07,801 --> 01:20:11,968
- [Tom] It was just a case
of mistaken identity, sorry.

2153
01:20:13,383 --> 01:20:14,266
- [Joel] Heck of a ride, huh?

2154
01:20:14,266 --> 01:20:15,099
Oof!

2155
01:20:15,099 --> 01:20:16,889
(soft jazz music)

2156
01:20:16,889 --> 01:20:18,126
- [Crow] Well at least
this vicious beating

2157
01:20:18,126 --> 01:20:20,209
has a cool accompaniment.

2158
01:20:21,795 --> 01:20:23,417
- [Tom] This'll teach you to make blintzes

2159
01:20:23,417 --> 01:20:25,334
out of super criminals.

2160
01:20:26,361 --> 01:20:29,561
- Now, let's begin with Lamas' number.

2161
01:20:29,561 --> 01:20:31,566
- [Crow] Fernando or Lorenzo?

2162
01:20:31,566 --> 01:20:33,998
- I'd like to know how you got hold of it.

2163
01:20:33,998 --> 01:20:36,729
- But I've told you it was Cooper.

2164
01:20:36,729 --> 01:20:37,625
- [All] Oooh!

2165
01:20:37,625 --> 01:20:38,734
- The dead don't talk.

2166
01:20:38,734 --> 01:20:41,465
- [Joel] You should see this
place around quittin' time.

2167
01:20:41,465 --> 01:20:43,001
- You are very beautiful.

2168
01:20:43,001 --> 01:20:45,262
- [Crow] She's sure wearing
a funny bathing suit.

2169
01:20:45,262 --> 01:20:47,822
- And it would be a pity to
have to put you in our tub.

2170
01:20:47,822 --> 01:20:49,315
- [Tom] For you see, the
Mr. Bubble may give you

2171
01:20:49,315 --> 01:20:51,491
a urinary infection.

2172
01:20:51,491 --> 01:20:54,009
- Tell me have you ever
had a bath in electricity?

2173
01:20:54,009 --> 01:20:55,950
- [Crow] Well once I saw
a bear eating a doughnut.

2174
01:20:55,950 --> 01:20:58,996
(electronic buzzing)

2175
01:20:58,996 --> 01:21:00,451
- [Joel] Hey George Wendt.

2176
01:21:00,451 --> 01:21:01,284
- [Tom] Went where?

2177
01:21:01,284 --> 01:21:02,117
Ha, another one, thank you.

2178
01:21:02,117 --> 01:21:03,867
- [Crow] D'oh, Servo.

2179
01:21:07,358 --> 01:21:08,691
- [All] Da-da-da-dum!

2180
01:21:08,691 --> 01:21:10,867
- [Tom] This is like The
Quiet Man only it takes place

2181
01:21:10,867 --> 01:21:14,494
in a mansion in Holland
with a couple of spies.

2182
01:21:14,494 --> 01:21:15,859
Sorry.

2183
01:21:15,859 --> 01:21:17,438
- [Crow] Now, now Gary,
this is the last time

2184
01:21:17,438 --> 01:21:19,579
you goin' to come home late.

2185
01:21:19,579 --> 01:21:21,875
(grunting)

2186
01:21:21,875 --> 01:21:25,656
- [Joel] Hey, he's got him in
a secret agent full dragon.

2187
01:21:25,656 --> 01:21:28,989
- [Crow] Sisyphus, what's he doing here?

2188
01:21:30,281 --> 01:21:31,433
- [Tom] All right.

2189
01:21:31,433 --> 01:21:35,187
Time to play the little
blintz game, mister.

2190
01:21:35,187 --> 01:21:36,297
- [Woman] Stop.

2191
01:21:36,297 --> 01:21:37,875
- You boys stop roughhousing in there.

2192
01:21:37,875 --> 01:21:39,375
- Wants him alive.

2193
01:21:41,246 --> 01:21:42,910
I thought you were 10 feet under, Bryan.

2194
01:21:42,910 --> 01:21:43,743
- [Crow] 10 feet under Bryan?

2195
01:21:43,743 --> 01:21:45,171
- Well you were wrong.

2196
01:21:45,171 --> 01:21:46,004
- [Joel] Dennis James?

2197
01:21:46,004 --> 01:21:47,310
- Like always.

2198
01:21:47,310 --> 01:21:48,505
- Not anymore.

2199
01:21:48,505 --> 01:21:50,169
Hands up.

2200
01:21:50,169 --> 01:21:53,966
- [Tom] Now Simon says put 'em down.

2201
01:21:53,966 --> 01:21:56,227
- [Crow] See, she wants me alive, told ya.

2202
01:21:56,227 --> 01:21:58,363
You would've gotten into a lot of trouble.

2203
01:21:58,363 --> 01:21:59,196
Live?

2204
01:22:01,945 --> 01:22:03,353
- [Joel] Oh come to think of it, I did

2205
01:22:03,353 --> 01:22:06,638
have a bath like that once, thanks though.

2206
01:22:06,638 --> 01:22:08,686
- [Man] This oughta refresh your memory.

2207
01:22:08,686 --> 01:22:09,710
- [Crow] And your pores.

2208
01:22:09,710 --> 01:22:10,543
- Coward.

2209
01:22:12,142 --> 01:22:14,475
- [Tom] Oh all of a sudden
they're at the Alamo.

2210
01:22:14,475 --> 01:22:16,323
(thuds)

2211
01:22:16,323 --> 01:22:18,585
- [Comfort] You'll pay for this.

2212
01:22:18,585 --> 01:22:19,418
We'll get even with you.

2213
01:22:19,418 --> 01:22:22,668
- [Crow] Uh, gee, can I have that cell?

2214
01:22:25,331 --> 01:22:26,398
(pistol fires)

2215
01:22:26,398 --> 01:22:29,398
- [Tom] Oh, right in the cummerbund.

2216
01:22:30,695 --> 01:22:31,945
(pistol fires)

2217
01:22:31,945 --> 01:22:34,528
- [Joel] Um, I'm with a client.

2218
01:22:36,169 --> 01:22:37,193
Sir, we don't take walk ins.

2219
01:22:37,193 --> 01:22:40,051
(pistol fires)
- [Crow] Ooh.

2220
01:22:40,051 --> 01:22:40,990
(pistol fires)

2221
01:22:40,990 --> 01:22:42,907
- [Crow] Whoa ho he ho.

2222
01:22:44,489 --> 01:22:47,325
- [Tom] It's my groommaid's dress.

2223
01:22:47,325 --> 01:22:48,716
- [Crow] Wait, wait, wait, who's alive?

2224
01:22:48,716 --> 01:22:50,466
Let's count off here.

2225
01:22:51,957 --> 01:22:54,790
(soft jazz music)

2226
01:22:55,796 --> 01:22:56,819
- [Joel] Hey it's not my gun,

2227
01:22:56,819 --> 01:23:00,069
check the powder burns, I didn't do it.

2228
01:23:01,001 --> 01:23:04,001
- [Tom] One last kiss would be nice.

2229
01:23:04,945 --> 01:23:07,486
- [Crow] You got a big
ball of wax in there.

2230
01:23:07,486 --> 01:23:09,363
- He must tell you.

2231
01:23:09,363 --> 01:23:10,196
Everything depends on it.

2232
01:23:10,196 --> 01:23:11,579
- It's alright, it's alright now,

2233
01:23:11,579 --> 01:23:13,853
don't speak anymore, don't speak anymore.

2234
01:23:13,853 --> 01:23:14,686
- [Joel] Alright?

2235
01:23:14,686 --> 01:23:16,519
You shot me, you jerk.

2236
01:23:17,470 --> 01:23:19,561
- [Crow] I can't believe I ever liked you.

2237
01:23:19,561 --> 01:23:20,755
- I couldn't help myself.

2238
01:23:20,755 --> 01:23:22,480
- [Crow] I ate the last
(speaking foreign language).

2239
01:23:22,480 --> 01:23:23,870
- It was the drug.

2240
01:23:23,870 --> 01:23:24,703
- I know.

2241
01:23:25,961 --> 01:23:27,710
I always knew.

2242
01:23:27,710 --> 01:23:28,649
- [Joel] I knew it was the drug,

2243
01:23:28,649 --> 01:23:31,649
you said it was the drug, I knew it.

2244
01:23:34,323 --> 01:23:35,987
- [Tom] Know what, it'd
be really bad if you died

2245
01:23:35,987 --> 01:23:38,820
while I was kissing you right now.

2246
01:23:40,851 --> 01:23:43,923
Now how does that make me feel?

2247
01:23:43,923 --> 01:23:48,090
- [Crow] He had to get every
last drop of love out of her.

2248
01:23:49,814 --> 01:23:51,433
- [Joel] Well,

2249
01:23:51,433 --> 01:23:52,755
I could still hug her,

2250
01:23:52,755 --> 01:23:54,377
that's not that weird, is it?

2251
01:23:54,377 --> 01:23:55,614
- [Crow] No.

2252
01:23:55,614 --> 01:23:56,851
- [Tom] Dead, huh?

2253
01:23:56,851 --> 01:23:59,851
Well, heh, best untie the other one.

2254
01:24:01,506 --> 01:24:05,591
- [Crow] (sighs) I just let myself out.

2255
01:24:05,591 --> 01:24:08,602
- [Tom] The haunting Herb
Alpert death theme here

2256
01:24:08,602 --> 01:24:10,769
on the music of your life.

2257
01:24:13,491 --> 01:24:14,899
- [Joel] Hey now wait a second,

2258
01:24:14,899 --> 01:24:17,982
two wrongs aren't gonna make a right.

2259
01:24:22,083 --> 01:24:24,916
- [Crow] Well, I'll do the honors.

2260
01:24:27,033 --> 01:24:28,910
Super Dragon worked the
deep fryers at Arby's.

2261
01:24:28,910 --> 01:24:31,257
He knows what he's doin.

2262
01:24:31,257 --> 01:24:34,030
- [Joel] They're gonna rust proof him.

2263
01:24:34,030 --> 01:24:35,353
- [Tom] Now would you guys scrub my back?

2264
01:24:35,353 --> 01:24:36,505
Oh, and there's a bottle
of Sardo someplace.

2265
01:24:36,505 --> 01:24:37,486
- Well.

2266
01:24:37,486 --> 01:24:38,319
- [Joel] Well.

2267
01:24:38,319 --> 01:24:39,790
- What have do you have to say to me, huh?

2268
01:24:39,790 --> 01:24:41,369
- I got nothing to say.

2269
01:24:41,369 --> 01:24:42,435
Just go to hell.

2270
01:24:42,435 --> 01:24:44,099
- That's very rude of you.

2271
01:24:44,099 --> 01:24:44,932
Comfort?

2272
01:24:45,806 --> 01:24:47,001
Teach him some manners.

2273
01:24:47,001 --> 01:24:48,323
- [Crow] Well the small
fork is for the shrimp

2274
01:24:48,323 --> 01:24:49,859
and keep your head below the queen.

2275
01:24:49,859 --> 01:24:51,442
- [Tom] No comfort.

2276
01:24:52,377 --> 01:24:55,193
- You won't make me talk.

2277
01:24:55,193 --> 01:24:56,193
- All right.

2278
01:24:59,161 --> 01:25:00,697
- [Tom] This'll be a shocking experience.

2279
01:25:00,697 --> 01:25:01,550
(laughs)

2280
01:25:01,550 --> 01:25:02,745
Watts for dinner?

2281
01:25:02,745 --> 01:25:04,793
- [Crow] Oh, Servo.

2282
01:25:04,793 --> 01:25:06,329
- [Joel] Oh I love it, increase the amps.

2283
01:25:06,329 --> 01:25:07,162
Come on.

2284
01:25:07,162 --> 01:25:10,329
(electricity buzzing)

2285
01:25:12,174 --> 01:25:14,435
- You have a beautiful voice, Salas.

2286
01:25:14,435 --> 01:25:16,355
Have you ever thought
about going on the stage?

2287
01:25:16,355 --> 01:25:17,519
- You'll both die for this.

2288
01:25:17,519 --> 01:25:19,772
- [Crow] Although I was in
Oliver in senior sketch night

2289
01:25:19,772 --> 01:25:21,714
and I had this little- (gargling)

2290
01:25:21,714 --> 01:25:24,214
- Make her stop it, I'll talk.

2291
01:25:25,714 --> 01:25:30,609
- [Joel] Hey it's Frank
the bodyguard's apartment.

2292
01:25:30,609 --> 01:25:32,241
- [Tom] What are they in Filene's Basement

2293
01:25:32,241 --> 01:25:33,574
all of a sudden?

2294
01:25:34,595 --> 01:25:36,199
- [Crow] Jeez, he should put
a fence around that thing,

2295
01:25:36,199 --> 01:25:38,401
he might run into problems when
he has a lot of people over,

2296
01:25:38,401 --> 01:25:41,499
they could get their head
crushed in or something.

2297
01:25:41,499 --> 01:25:43,278
- [Joel] Oh, it's still working anyway.

2298
01:25:43,278 --> 01:25:45,861
I haven't been home in a while.

2299
01:25:47,134 --> 01:25:48,416
- [Crow] Used to have handles on it.

2300
01:25:48,416 --> 01:25:49,249
You could just open it.

2301
01:25:49,249 --> 01:25:52,043
It was actually more convenient.

2302
01:25:52,043 --> 01:25:53,457
Same deal here, pretty much.

2303
01:25:53,457 --> 01:25:57,624
More for show really, I can
get you one if you want one.

2304
01:25:58,700 --> 01:26:00,114
- [Joel] Boy, you're really proud of that

2305
01:26:00,114 --> 01:26:02,197
clay squirrel, aren't ya?

2306
01:26:03,588 --> 01:26:07,170
- I'm very happy to see you again.

2307
01:26:07,170 --> 01:26:09,233
- [Tom] I was being facetious.

2308
01:26:09,233 --> 01:26:10,653
- Can I give you a hand?

2309
01:26:10,653 --> 01:26:11,851
- [Crow] Why sure, you can help us.

2310
01:26:11,851 --> 01:26:14,709
(pistol fires)

2311
01:26:14,709 --> 01:26:17,376
- [Joel] Just come right in Ray.

2312
01:26:20,231 --> 01:26:22,240
- [Tom] He said can I give you a hand.

2313
01:26:22,240 --> 01:26:25,240
(laughing)

2314
01:26:25,240 --> 01:26:27,452
- He was the only one left
who could tell you the formula

2315
01:26:27,452 --> 01:26:29,047
for Anti-Synchron.

2316
01:26:29,047 --> 01:26:30,592
- [Crow] Did it have mushroom soup in it?

2317
01:26:30,592 --> 01:26:32,369
- Now your mission is failed, Cooper.

2318
01:26:32,369 --> 01:26:34,132
Failed totally.

2319
01:26:34,132 --> 01:26:36,742
As for me, I couldn't tell
you now, even if I wanted to.

2320
01:26:36,742 --> 01:26:39,909
- [Joel] This is my headshot you know?

2321
01:26:41,599 --> 01:26:42,849
- [Crow] You hear that Elizabeth?

2322
01:26:42,849 --> 01:26:44,060
I'm coming to join you, honey.

2323
01:26:44,060 --> 01:26:45,218
- I don't need the formula.

2324
01:26:45,218 --> 01:26:47,121
I already photographed it in your office

2325
01:26:47,121 --> 01:26:48,576
with this camera, look.

2326
01:26:48,576 --> 01:26:49,480
See, huh, huh?

2327
01:26:49,480 --> 01:26:51,625
- [Tom] So you're killing
yourself for nothing.

2328
01:26:51,625 --> 01:26:53,737
Na, na, na, na, na, na.

2329
01:26:53,737 --> 01:26:54,570
- [Joel] What a jerk,

2330
01:26:54,570 --> 01:26:55,855
he just wanted to get the guy's goat

2331
01:26:55,855 --> 01:26:57,158
right before he died.

2332
01:26:57,158 --> 01:26:58,209
- The boys at Fremont are saved

2333
01:26:58,209 --> 01:27:00,368
and there's loads of
decorations pouring in for you.

2334
01:27:00,368 --> 01:27:02,212
We're just waiting for you to get back.

2335
01:27:02,212 --> 01:27:04,026
- [Cooper] Yeah, well
when are you expecting me?

2336
01:27:04,026 --> 01:27:05,603
- [Crow] Senator Hawlings,
get off the line.

2337
01:27:05,603 --> 01:27:06,616
- Right away of course.

2338
01:27:06,616 --> 01:27:07,813
- [Cooper] Well don't hold your breath.

2339
01:27:07,813 --> 01:27:08,951
- What?

2340
01:27:08,951 --> 01:27:10,671
I don't understand.

2341
01:27:10,671 --> 01:27:12,608
- Yeah you heard me all right.

2342
01:27:12,608 --> 01:27:14,286
I'm taking a little vacation.

2343
01:27:14,286 --> 01:27:15,161
- [Charity] Why?

2344
01:27:15,161 --> 01:27:15,994
- Why?

2345
01:27:15,994 --> 01:27:16,973
- [Tom] I had the time comin'.

2346
01:27:16,973 --> 01:27:18,787
- Holland is beautiful in the fall.

2347
01:27:18,787 --> 01:27:19,824
- [Charity] What about Babyface?

2348
01:27:19,824 --> 01:27:20,854
- Oh Babyface?

2349
01:27:20,854 --> 01:27:22,113
- [Crow] He's beautiful anytime.

2350
01:27:22,113 --> 01:27:23,321
- Yeah, I know I gotta send
him right back to Sing Sing,

2351
01:27:23,321 --> 01:27:25,458
but I'm afraid I can't do that right now.

2352
01:27:25,458 --> 01:27:28,148
He seems to be very, very busy

2353
01:27:28,148 --> 01:27:29,979
absorbing the local color.

2354
01:27:29,979 --> 01:27:33,595
- [Joel] Appears he's
adopted a Dutch family.

2355
01:27:33,595 --> 01:27:35,183
- Now listen, you made a deal with Coleman

2356
01:27:35,183 --> 01:27:36,433
to bring him back now.

2357
01:27:36,433 --> 01:27:37,642
You can't break your word.

2358
01:27:37,642 --> 01:27:39,092
A deal is a deal, do you hear?

2359
01:27:39,092 --> 01:27:40,782
Now you and Babyface
get on the first plane--

2360
01:27:40,782 --> 01:27:41,693
- [Tom] Flint!

2361
01:27:41,693 --> 01:27:42,570
- Well I'm very sorry

2362
01:27:42,570 --> 01:27:44,182
but there's nothing I can do about that.

2363
01:27:44,182 --> 01:27:46,328
(Tom mimicking sped up voice)

2364
01:27:46,328 --> 01:27:48,599
- I'm going to be very busy too.

2365
01:27:48,599 --> 01:27:50,553
Studying the local customs.

2366
01:27:50,553 --> 01:27:54,462
- [Joel] (chuckles) How about
a little Dutch treat, huh?

2367
01:27:54,462 --> 01:27:56,191
- [Crow] At least the
movie had a good payoff.

2368
01:27:56,191 --> 01:27:57,024
- Yeah.

2369
01:27:57,936 --> 01:28:00,603
(doors closing)

2370
01:28:05,575 --> 01:28:07,955
Okay, no, no, no, it's very simple.

2371
01:28:07,955 --> 01:28:08,949
- Simple.
- [Joel] Secret.

2372
01:28:08,949 --> 01:28:10,374
- Secret simple
- [Joel] Agent.

2373
01:28:10,374 --> 01:28:12,183
- Agent thing.
- Super Dragon.

2374
01:28:12,183 --> 01:28:14,593
- Secret Super Dragon lady thing.

2375
01:28:14,593 --> 01:28:16,105
- Alright, knock it off you mutton heads.

2376
01:28:16,105 --> 01:28:17,859
We gotta do that super
villain conference call

2377
01:28:17,859 --> 01:28:18,898
with Dr. Forrester.

2378
01:28:18,898 --> 01:28:20,861
- Super villain deal, aw forget it.

2379
01:28:20,861 --> 01:28:22,575
- Come in, your surliness.

2380
01:28:22,575 --> 01:28:24,197
- Sing, sing, sing.

2381
01:28:24,197 --> 01:28:25,393
Oh hi Joel.

2382
01:28:25,393 --> 01:28:28,976
Dr. Forrester'll be
with you in one minute.

2383
01:28:32,053 --> 01:28:33,505
- Ah Mr. Robinson,

2384
01:28:33,505 --> 01:28:36,487
why don't you introduce your colleagues?

2385
01:28:36,487 --> 01:28:38,540
- Well sirs, pretty
much the same colleagues

2386
01:28:38,540 --> 01:28:40,198
as I always have.

2387
01:28:40,198 --> 01:28:41,394
Uh, Tom Servo,

2388
01:28:41,394 --> 01:28:42,357
Crow T. Robot,

2389
01:28:42,357 --> 01:28:43,641
Gypsy couldn't make it.

2390
01:28:43,641 --> 01:28:44,614
- [Tom and Crow] Hi.

2391
01:28:44,614 --> 01:28:46,732
- Well thank you for coming by today.

2392
01:28:46,732 --> 01:28:48,536
Our topic is super villains

2393
01:28:48,536 --> 01:28:50,106
and I think I'd like to open it up to

2394
01:28:50,106 --> 01:28:51,417
question and answer.

2395
01:28:51,417 --> 01:28:52,315
Well thank you, Frank.

2396
01:28:52,315 --> 01:28:53,148
- Whatever.

2397
01:28:53,148 --> 01:28:53,981
- Can I get some cream?

2398
01:28:53,981 --> 01:28:54,814
- No.

2399
01:28:54,814 --> 01:28:55,647
- Great, Joel?

2400
01:28:55,647 --> 01:28:58,790
- Well I think the question
our field reps ask most

2401
01:28:58,790 --> 01:29:01,355
at this week's movie meeting was,

2402
01:29:01,355 --> 01:29:03,429
why the super villain in today's film

2403
01:29:03,429 --> 01:29:06,057
failed to make any kind of
an impression, gentlemen?

2404
01:29:06,057 --> 01:29:08,418
- Right, pretty much,
no impression at all.

2405
01:29:08,418 --> 01:29:10,281
- Ah very good.

2406
01:29:10,281 --> 01:29:15,062
Well perhaps one reason why
this super villain failed

2407
01:29:15,062 --> 01:29:18,312
and I believe the 1971 Dr. No monograph

2408
01:29:20,035 --> 01:29:21,729
will back me up here,

2409
01:29:21,729 --> 01:29:24,291
is that he did not possess

2410
01:29:24,291 --> 01:29:26,374
a strange or rare animal.

2411
01:29:28,353 --> 01:29:31,353
I can't be too strong on this point.

2412
01:29:32,823 --> 01:29:34,823
Either four legs or two.

2413
01:29:36,422 --> 01:29:39,755
Every super villain must have an animal.

2414
01:29:41,027 --> 01:29:43,523
Frank, I believe you had a question.

2415
01:29:43,523 --> 01:29:44,356
- Oh yeah.

2416
01:29:46,614 --> 01:29:47,534
Eagerly,

2417
01:29:47,534 --> 01:29:51,044
I've always thought it would
be easy and fun to start up

2418
01:29:51,044 --> 01:29:54,105
a super villain franchise, is that true?

2419
01:29:54,105 --> 01:29:56,036
- Ah, excellent question, very good.

2420
01:29:56,036 --> 01:29:57,558
Uh no, no,

2421
01:29:57,558 --> 01:29:59,166
it is

2422
01:29:59,166 --> 01:30:00,794
not

2423
01:30:00,794 --> 01:30:01,627
easy

2424
01:30:03,269 --> 01:30:05,854
to set up a super villain franchise.

2425
01:30:05,854 --> 01:30:07,926
You see today's super villain,

2426
01:30:07,926 --> 01:30:12,246
is in essence the small
business owner of his franchise.

2427
01:30:12,246 --> 01:30:13,928
He does the purchasing,

2428
01:30:13,928 --> 01:30:15,845
the hiring, the firing,

2429
01:30:16,756 --> 01:30:21,345
plus must maintain medical
and dental and benefits for

2430
01:30:21,345 --> 01:30:24,986
an unstable and terribly
dishonest group of henchmen.

2431
01:30:24,986 --> 01:30:26,986
But if you are dedicated

2432
01:30:27,895 --> 01:30:30,362
and are not afraid of a little hard work,

2433
01:30:30,362 --> 01:30:34,695
then you'll find that the
field of super villainry

2434
01:30:34,695 --> 01:30:37,626
can be very rewarding indeed.

2435
01:30:37,626 --> 01:30:39,184
Yes, next question.

2436
01:30:39,184 --> 01:30:41,229
- Well the only thing we wanted to ask

2437
01:30:41,229 --> 01:30:44,235
and I think we're all
in agreement on this is-

2438
01:30:44,235 --> 01:30:46,736
- [All] What do ya think sirs?

2439
01:30:46,736 --> 01:30:48,116
- Good question.

2440
01:30:48,116 --> 01:30:49,949
Push the button Frank.

2441
01:30:51,718 --> 01:30:52,885
What the, hey.

2442
01:30:54,248 --> 01:30:57,665
(epic synthesizer music)

2443
01:31:56,608 --> 01:31:58,858
(grunting)

